# Skills

Personal skills and user-level agent rules are versioned in `~/Code/dotfiles/agents/`.

| Kind | Write here |
| --- | --- |
| Personal skill | `~/Code/dotfiles/agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` |
| User-level rule | `~/Code/dotfiles/agents/rules/<name>.mdc` |

When creating or updating a **personal/global** skill or user-level rule, write
it in those dotfiles paths. App discovery paths are symlinks to these files;
do not create a second copy outside the repo.

Laravel Boost and other framework guideline skills belong here too: testing,
Laravel, Livewire, Volt, Horizon, Fortify, Flux, Tailwind, Pest, Inertia, and
the same kind of package skill. Do not keep a second copy in a project's
`.cursor/skills`, `.github/skills`, or `.agents/skills`. If Boost installs
them into a project, move them into dotfiles and remove the project copy.

Project skills and project rules still belong in the current repository.
Never write into app-managed built-in skill directories.

Re-run `~/Code/dotfiles/agents/link.zsh` if a link is missing or was replaced by
a real directory. Start a new task to reload global instructions; restart the
app if a new skill does not appear.
